name: engine-driven-rear-spin
description: >
  Engine-on, rear paddock stand, 1st gear. Hold the throttle at several
  RPM setpoints with the clutch fully out — engine drives the rear
  wheel through the gearbox. Steady-state speeds let us read 12D D2,
  D3, D5, D6 at constant operating points: pins byte-to-km/h scaling
  via RPM × known gearing, surfaces the D3/D5 high bytes if the uint16
  hypothesis holds, and disambiguates D2 vs D6.
experiment: 2026-06-23-engine-driven-rear-spin

# Timing convention: marks fire at STEP START — the moment the rider is
# cued to start holding the throttle at the named setpoint. Bus broadcast
# is keyed off the actual throttle position; the dash/rider visual is
# secondary. Analysis windows are the held steady-state portion, not the
# transients.
#
# Setpoints are RPM targets in 1st gear, chosen against the KTM 390
# platform gearing (primary 80/30, 1st 32/12, final 45/15 → 21.33:1
# total) and 150/60ZR17 rear (~1.922 m circumference). At those ratios:
#   2000 RPM → 10.8 km/h (below both byte ceilings)
#   2500 RPM → 13.5 km/h (still below)
#   3500 RPM → 18.9 km/h (past D6's 16 km/h ceiling → D5 emerges)
#   4500 RPM → 24.3 km/h (D5 stays on, D2 still single-byte)
#   5500 RPM → 29.7 km/h (past D2's 25.5 km/h ceiling → D3 emerges)
# Two setpoints below all ceilings (clean single-byte regression), one
# crossing D5's ceiling, one above D5 but below D3, one crossing D3's.
# Rider holds each by feel against the tach — drift ±200 RPM is fine
# because the analysis reads RPM from CAN frame-by-frame anyway.
#
# Rests between holds are at IDLE (engine running, clutch out, gear in,
# wheel turning at idle speed) — keeps the data clean rather than going
# clutch-in then clutch-out repeatedly. Idle-in-gear is itself a useful
# data point, so we hold a long idle-in-gear settle first.
#
# Engine cooling: no airflow, so high RPM holds are short (~10 s) and
# return-to-idle rests are longer (~10 s). The rider should watch the
# coolant temp on the dash and abort if it approaches fan-on territory.

steps:
  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- Setup
  - prompt: "Bike on rear paddock stand, FRONT WHEEL STRAIGHT and braced. Key OFF, neutral, kill RUN. Hands clear. Recording silence."
    duration_secs: 6

  - prompt: "Turn key ON. Confirm dash boots normally. Hands off."
    duration_secs: 30
    countdown_from: 3
    mark: { key: mark, label: "key on" }

  - prompt: "Press STARTER. Let it catch — throttle closed."
    duration_secs: 10
    countdown_from: 3
    mark: { key: start, label: "starter pressed" }

  - prompt: "Idle settle — engine on, NEUTRAL, hands off. Clean idle baseline."
    duration_secs: 30
    mark: { key: idle_settled, label: "idle settled (neutral)" }

  # ----------------------------------- Phase A — Engage 1st, idle-in-gear baseline
  - prompt: >
      PHASE A — Clutch IN. Shift to 1st. Bring clutch SLOWLY out until
      the rear wheel starts turning at idle. Throttle CLOSED. Both
      feet ready. Left hand stays off the bike for the rest of the
      session — throttle only with the right hand.
    duration_secs: 15

  - prompt: "Idle-in-gear hold — clutch fully out, throttle CLOSED, hands clear of chain. Reading rear wheel at idle through 1st."
    duration_secs: 15
    countdown_from: 3
    mark: { key: setpoint, label: "Phase A — idle in 1st" }

  # ----------------------------------- Phase B — RPM setpoint sweep (1st gear)
  - prompt: >
      PHASE B — RPM sweep in 1st gear. Five throttle setpoints, ~10 s
      hold each, returning to idle-in-gear between. Watch coolant temp
      on the dash — if it climbs unexpectedly, abort.
    duration_secs: 10

  - prompt: "Bring RPM to ~2000 and hold steady. Dash tach is your guide."
    duration_secs: 12
    countdown_from: 3
    mark: { key: setpoint, label: "B1 — ~2000 RPM in 1st" }

  - prompt: "Return to idle-in-gear (throttle CLOSED). Engine cool down."
    duration_secs: 10

  - prompt: "Bring RPM to ~2500 and hold steady."
    duration_secs: 12
    countdown_from: 3
    mark: { key: setpoint, label: "B2 — ~2500 RPM in 1st" }

  - prompt: "Return to idle-in-gear. Cool down."
    duration_secs: 10

  - prompt: "Bring RPM to ~3500 and hold steady."
    duration_secs: 12
    countdown_from: 3
    mark: { key: setpoint, label: "B3 — ~3500 RPM in 1st" }

  - prompt: "Return to idle-in-gear. Cool down — extra time, engine is warming up."
    duration_secs: 15

  - prompt: "Bring RPM to ~4500 and hold steady."
    duration_secs: 12
    countdown_from: 3
    mark: { key: setpoint, label: "B4 — ~4500 RPM in 1st" }

  - prompt: "Return to idle-in-gear. Cool down."
    duration_secs: 15

  - prompt: "Bring RPM to ~5500 and hold steady. Final setpoint."
    duration_secs: 12
    countdown_from: 3
    mark: { key: setpoint, label: "B5 — ~5500 RPM in 1st" }

  - prompt: "Return to idle-in-gear. Cool down."
    duration_secs: 15

  # ----------------------------------- Phase C — Re-baseline idle-in-gear
  - prompt: "Idle-in-gear re-baseline — confirms readings haven't drifted across the sweep (thermal, ABS-fault-related, etc.)."
    duration_secs: 15
    countdown_from: 3
    mark: { key: setpoint, label: "Phase C — idle in 1st (post-sweep)" }

  # ----------------------------------------------------------- Shutdown
  - prompt: "Clutch IN. Shift to NEUTRAL. Clutch OUT. Confirm N indicator."
    duration_secs: 12
    countdown_from: 3
    mark: { key: mark, label: "back to neutral" }

  - prompt: "Idle settle in neutral. Hands off."
    duration_secs: 10

  - prompt: "Kill switch → STOP. Let decay finish."
    duration_secs: 12
    countdown_from: 3
    mark: { key: kill, label: "kill switch" }

  - prompt: "Key OFF when silent. Hold 3 s of tail silence."
    duration_secs: 6

  - prompt: "Done. Press q to stop capture and fill in session.md (note ABS lamp behaviour, any dash anomalies, actual RPM held vs target per setpoint, coolant temp at session end)."
    duration_secs: null
